681 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (The Poverty Proofing Libraries programme has demonstrated that while libraries are highly valued as inclusive, community-based spaces, there remain a range of visible and hidden barriers that can prevent full and equitable access for children, young people and families experiencing poverty.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
682 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Through engagement with library staff, users and non-users, this work has highlighted that small, often unintentional factors - such as unclear costs, limited communication, lack of targeted activities or assumptions about behaviour - can significantly influence whether individuals feel able, confident and welcome to engage. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
683 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (At the same time, the findings reinforce the powerful role libraries already play as trusted, supportive environments that promote connection, learning and wellbeing.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
684 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 201 0 R
/T (Conclusion)
/E (Conclusion)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Importantly, this programme shows that meaningful change is both achievable and impactful. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (Where libraries have reflected on these findings and taken action, improvements in accessibility, inclusivity and engagement have already been realised.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E ( Embedding a poverty-informed approach is not about large-scale transformation, but about consistent, practical changes rooted in empathy, dignity and lived experience.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
